00:06:15.630 --> 00:06:18.690
Hopefully by now you'll be able to tell
that that difference usually implies that

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.039
someone is not being completely honest.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:25.660
The third thing to look for
is the positioning of the palms.

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:29.070
Will you believe me more if I'm
talking to you like this, or

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:29.860
if I'm talking to you like this?

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:35.720
Our palms are a part of our body that we
use to connect with other people a lot.

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:39.480
That's why we handshake, that's why
we wave whenever we greet people.

00:06:39.480 --> 00:06:42.910
Therefore, whenever someone is lying,
it's very hard to do so

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:45.290
with their palms exposed.

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:48.820
So, what we do is we either put them
in our pockets, or just put them,

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:53.010
facing down, or we put them behind
an object that may be in between us and

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:54.890
the people that we're lying to,
such as a desk.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:07:00.540
Gesturing is the most primitive way
of communication that humans have.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:06.230
And for that reason, we tend to
do the movements instantaneously.

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:09.743
Even when we can rehearse
the words that we say when we lie,

00:07:09.743 --> 00:07:12.460
the gestures have a mind of their own.

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:13.960
So they're more involuntary.

00:07:15.570 --> 00:07:19.360
By now, hopefully you'll be able to
see that if you pay attention to where

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:24.060
the hands go, the timing of the movement
and also, where the palms are facing.

00:07:25.390 --> 00:07:27.330
We'd say a lot without saying nothing.

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:33.020
&gt;&gt; Well,
Daniel just showed us the importance of

00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:35.960
looking at the hand
gestures to detect lies.

00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:39.180
And Rodolphe had mentioned
the facial expression.

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:43.060
Joe Navarro who's been an FBI
behavioral analyst for

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:47.940
the past 20 years and
author of What Everybody Is Saying,

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:51.520
claims that the most honest part
of our body is actually our feet.

00:07:52.790 --> 00:07:57.831
And this is because when we try to
control our body we focus on our facial

00:07:57.831 --> 00:08:02.538
expressions and our hands but
we often don't rehearse our feet.

00:08:02.538 --> 00:08:06.839
So there's really four main things that
you should look out for with the feet.

00:08:06.839 --> 00:08:11.300
The first is how you stand.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:16.230
So I'm standing here with my weight
equally distributed between both my legs.

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:20.650
This shows that I'm much more
comfortable about what I'm saying.

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:26.679
And I'm taking a firm stand on the
subject, but if I were to cross my legs,

00:08:26.679 --> 00:08:30.879
this is a much more closed and
defensive position.

00:08:30.879 --> 00:08:34.300
I'm much more uncomfortable
about what I'm saying and

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:36.780
I'm likely to be more nervous about it.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:40.550
And I were to shift my
weight from side to side.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.540
Or rock back and forth.

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:47.740
This is a sign that I'm
trying to calm myself.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:50.190
And again, I'm likely nervous
about what I'm saying to you.

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:55.530
The second thing to look out for,
is how often the feet are moving.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:59.390
So, if I'm fidgeting my feet,
if I'm tapping them,

00:08:59.390 --> 00:09:02.050
if I'm winding them around things.

00:09:02.050 --> 00:09:05.120
It's likely another sign that I'm
uncomfortable with what I'm saying to you.

00:09:07.020 --> 00:09:12.409
The third thing to look out for is the
direction of where my feet are pointing.

00:09:12.409 --> 00:09:15.835
This is an indication of
my interest level and

00:09:15.835 --> 00:09:19.770
my liking towards the person
that I'm talking to.

00:09:19.770 --> 00:09:24.480
So if we were to have a conversation and
my feet were pointing toward the door but

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:29.440
my torso is still pointed towards you,
it likely means that I wanna exit this

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:32.305
conversation because I'm not
interested in talking to you.

00:09:32.305 --> 00:09:36.200
[LAUGH] And the fourth and
final thing to look out for

00:09:36.200 --> 00:09:41.200
is this concept of ankle locking and
this is where one ankle crosses the other.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:45.869
And this is a sign that somebody is
likely withholding information from you.

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:49.220
For example, in therapy sessions,

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:53.910
a lot of patients will lock their ankles
as they're withholding their emotions.

00:09:55.150 --> 00:10:00.100
And in negotiations, if the person
across from the table from you is

00:10:00.100 --> 00:10:05.120
locking their ankles, it likely means that
they're withholding valuable concessions.

00:10:06.660 --> 00:10:11.575
So for all these reasons,
remember that one of the most honest,

00:10:11.575 --> 00:10:15.220
non-verbal communicators
are actually your feet.

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:18.960
So take a glance down at somebody's
feet when you're talking to them.

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:21.897
And look out for the four signs of lying.

00:10:21.897 --> 00:10:24.910
Unbalanced stance,

00:10:24.910 --> 00:10:30.440
lot of feet movement, the feet pointing
away from you, and ankle locking.

00:10:30.440 --> 00:10:36.173
&gt;&gt; So at this point we've really picked
apart the nonverbals of deception.

00:10:36.173 --> 00:10:40.810
We've talked to you about the face,
we've talked to you about the hands, and

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:42.310
we've talked to you about the feet.

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:44.990
Just to bring it back together,

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:48.580
it's important to remember to
view behaviors in clusters.

00:10:48.580 --> 00:10:52.690
So look for at least three signs
of lying before calling foul.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:57.330
And if you can, think about
the context of what's normal for

00:10:57.330 --> 00:10:58.520
the individual that you're observing.

00:10:59.630 --> 00:11:05.150
Now, we don't condone lying per se, but we
would encourage you to use this knowledge,

00:11:05.150 --> 00:11:06.520
not only for others, but for yourself.

00:11:07.530 --> 00:11:10.940
So the next time you're at
the World Series of Poker,

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:14.700
don't forget your sunglasses to
cover up those dilated pupils.

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:17.390
Or if that's not in the cards,

00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:21.660
consider your next tough negotiation,
or interview situation.

00:11:22.960 --> 00:11:24.830
We'd love now to turn to questions,

00:11:24.830 --> 00:11:27.410
would love to hear anything
that you would like to ask us,

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:31.239
but first we want to answer what might be
the most burning question in the room.

00:11:32.930 --> 00:11:33.492
Who was lying?

00:11:33.492 --> 00:11:37.726
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]

